From 78dbbcd7383df9feb051b8f5e77a8abac8157e5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: swackhamer <swackhamer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 15:08:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] PROBE (never land): OXIDEX_PROBE_SILENCE drops rows per
 generated-data class

A measurement probe for the OBSERVED axis of "how much of oxidex's matched
output comes from generated tables". Not a feature; this branch is never
merged anywhere.

OXIDEX_PROBE_SILENCE (read once per process, comma-separated) drops rows at
each class's outward boundary as scout.md mapped it, leaving internal walk
state (SetMember/DataMember, cipher ctx, value_form, descents) intact:

  engine              engine.rs / ifd_engine.rs Emitted pushes
  legacy-l1           runtime::DecodedField::emit -> None (RawAccess rows kept)
  legacy-l2           binary_subdir, canon custom_functions2, infiray,
                      sony main_extra, sony walker over minolta_a100 TABLES
  legacy-l3           sony walker over plain/enciphered, nikon encrypted
                      (value_form kept), nikon settings, canon binary_tables,
                      camera_info, filter_info, color_data, canon_vrd VER1
  producers-identity  generated File:FileType/FileTypeExtension/MIMEType writes
  producers-composite the 3 generated_compute Composite arms
  producers-dicom / -geotiff / -fits   rows named by the generated tables
  composite-declared  every Composite::apply row (hybrid bound, not in producers)
  legacy = l1+l2+l3; producers = the five producers-* tokens

conv is refused (exit 2): no clean choke point, a silenced PrintConv lookup
yields a wrong value rather than an absent row. Unknown tokens exit 2.

Unset or empty: byte-identical `oxidex -j` output to afd3a628's release
binary on the 82-file bounded subset (only File:FileAccessDate differs, which
also differs between two runs of the tip binary itself).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
